course: dictionary
lesson: 2308
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: they are its context. «The frogs croaked all night by the pond.» Frogs and a pond are the clues, so croak means a deep, rough sound.
explain: Croak can also be about a voice. «She had a sore throat and could only croak out a reply.» The clue is the sore throat, so croak here means to speak in a deep, rough voice. Try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Slang is a special kind of word that people use in jokes and casual talk. «Croaked» can mean died, but it is rough and joking, so it is not polite. Cartoons may use it for a pretend villain, but it can hurt when a real person has died.
fact: Croak is a verb (you croak) and a noun (a croak is the sound).
fact: «Croak» means a deep, rough sound, like the sound a frog or crow makes.
fact: Frogs and toads croak, especially to attract mates.
fact: «Croak out» means to say something in a rough voice, for example with a sore throat.
fact: «Croaked» means died, but it is rough slang and not polite; it is not a kind word to use about a real person.
exercise: «The frog began to croak by the pond.» What does croak mean here? | *A deep, rough sound | Sing a happy tune | Fall asleep | Run very fast
exercise: «She had a sore throat, so she could only croak out a reply.» What does croak out mean? | *Say something with a rough voice | Laugh at a joke | Shout very loudly | Write a note
exercise: Why is it not kind to say «croaked» about a real person who has died? | It is a polite word | *It is a joking word, hurtful at a real funeral | It means happy | It is too long
test: Which word is the rough sound a frog makes? | Splash | *Croak | Sing | Hop
test: Which sentence uses croak as a noun? | The frog will croak tonight. | *The toad gave a loud croak. | The toad jumped away. | The toad is green and wet.
exam: Which best describes «croaked» as slang? | A polite word for sleeping | *A joking, not polite, way to say someone died | A word for a happy song | A kind word for a doctor
